 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not cheesy is relative, but The thriller from St. Elsa in Ice Smart Pop last year is a good basic rhythm. It's pop dance, not necessarily the first dance at a big event. Then look at what they' playing now, rather than what you remember from before. Most jazz bars play something you can dance to, even if it' not exactly what you'd think. It is. Lots of people dance to stuff they wouldn't normally, just because it' being played. It can be, depending on who you want. Roughly what you'd pay for a night out yourself, maybe a bit less. Think of it as a shared music experience with others. Go for the basic rhythm I mentioned, and pick a song you actually like. People will dance to that, and it's easy to lead.",
